<title>UK: LME copper edges back in evening trade.</title>
<headline>LME copper edges back in evening trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Copper prices eased slightly during London Metal Exchange evening trade on Tuesday.</p>
<p>At 1800 GMT the red metal was indicated at $2,297/$2,298 just a couple of dollars under the $2,300 kerb close, down $19.</p>
<p>But zinc continued to firm and was indicated at $1,546/$1,550 and aluminium also held gains at $1,621/$1,632.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 8058</p>
</text>
